      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 9,
          "section": "4.1. The origin of deformation bands",
          "quote": "In addition, a few needle-shaped phases were observed in the same coarse grain ( Fig. 10d), which were also arranged in a parallel orientation. The SAED pattern of this site indicated two co-existing BCC phases with similar crystal parameters (a ¼ 332.3pm), and an orientation of {01 1} BCC1k{110} BCC2, <011> BCC1k<001> BCC2 (Fig. 10 e). Elemental line scanning of this region indicated spinodal decomposition between Nb and Ti/V. One of the decomposed phases was Nb-rich, with a disordered BCC structure (typically referred to as the A2 phase) based on the SAED identiﬁcation. Moreover, the composition of this A2 phase ﬂuctuated along the separation direction, and was approximately Ti27eV23eNb46eZr4.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 10",
          "chunk_id": "f523f839d0e8433a:part:001"
        }
      ]
